                                "sense_id": "07a8bf80-b9d9-308c-8296-16f3ec120ff7",
                                "text": "We see such gold ox-heads figured both in the inventories on the clay tablets at Knossos and on the Tomb of Rekhmara, as part of the tribute brought by the Keftians, the men of the isles in the midst of the sea, to the Egypt of the early fifteenth century."
